  "blocking_findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "PV3-B001",
      "severity": "BLOCKING",
      "title": "T4 added-event attribution scope and denominator do not cover every condition that requires F_auto or F_replica",
      "affected_components": [
        "T4 Level-A worker policy selection",
        "T4 conditional Level-B policy scoring",
        "T4 cross-target verifier row and diagonal",
        "F_LEVEL_B_SURFACES when T4 is selected",
        "F_CROSS_TARGET_8X8",
        "Grade C",
        "advancement specificity and ranking",
        "C2-G5",
        "C2-G8"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        "The T4 observation contract says primary formal attribution applies only to Level-A d=+1.5 versus paired sham and separately says a Level-B d>0 cell uses the identical classifier descriptively.",
        "The same contract's denominator says to pool all ADDED events from the +1.5 versus sham comparison, without an exact context-indexed replacement rule for other positive doses or verifier executions.",
        "The Level-A T4 worker policy considers d=[0.5,1.0,1.5] and defines every positive-dose C4 using F_auto(u) and the attribution denominator, leaving d=0.5 and d=1.0 outside the stated Level-A attribution scope.",
        "The Level-B T4 policy considers the positive cells d=0.75 and d=1.5 across carriers 11-15 Hz and defines C4 using F_auto(u), while the literal denominator remains +1.5 versus sham.",
        "The verifier freezes whichever positive Level-A T4 dose wins, requires pooled attribution and F_replica for a T4-packet condition, and recomputes diagonal G4, but the observation contract does not name verifier attribution as a comparison context."
      ],
      "impact": "Conforming implementations can omit attribution for Level-A d=0.5 or d=1.0, reuse the +1.5 pool for other cells, or generalize per condition. These choices can change C4, the selected T4 policy, Level-B bands, T4 benefit/adverse members, the full 128-member matrix, Grade C, advancement, and future C2 gates. Full cross-file executability and complete PV2-B002 closure therefore fail before outcomes.",
      "minimal_prospective_next_version_repair": [
        "Freeze one explicit attribution-domain table covering Level-A worker, conditional Level B, and cross-target verifier contexts for every positive T4 policy candidate, or prospectively constrain every T4 policy to the already defined +1.5 condition.",
        "For each retained context and condition, freeze the exact paired sham, pooling unit, dose and carrier binding, emitted-packet table, N_added and contributing-block denominator, F_auto and F_replica, missingness, bootstrap behavior, and required log fields.",
        "Replace the literal +1.5-only denominator text with an exact context-indexed rule while preserving +1.5 as the formal F_TARGET_DECISIONS comparison, unless all non-+1.5 candidates are removed consistently.",
        "Harmonize control_target_registry.json, mechanistic_parameter_map.json, phase2_protocol.json, advancement_rule.json, c2_gate_protocol.json, claim_registry.json, and the design memo; bind them in a new immutable freeze with new hashes.",
        "Declare Candidate V3 stale for implementation and obtain a new independent outcome-blind protocol re-audit before code inspection, implementation, preflight, verifier execution, or scientific outcomes."
      ]
    }
